  "keys": "აეილმნორსუ",
  "grammar": {
    "explain": [
      "Georgian has its own alphabet, *mkhedruli*: 33 round, curly letters, used only for Georgian and its sister languages. It looks hard, but it is one of the most regular alphabets in the world:",
      {
        "ul": [
          "One letter, one sound: every letter is always read the same way, and every sound has its own letter. Once you know the letters, you can read any word aloud.",
          "No capital letters: a sentence or a name starts with the same letter as any other word.",
          "It is written from left to right, like English.",
          "Every letter is pronounced, also at the end of a word: there are no silent letters."
        ]
      },
      "The writing of Georgian is so special that UNESCO lists it as part of the world's cultural heritage. In this lesson you learn the five vowels and five consonants: with them you can already read your first words.",
      {
        "h": "The vowels"
      },
      "Georgian vowels are short and clear, as in Italian or Spanish. Tap each letter to see how it sounds and a word that has it.",
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "ა",
            "latin": "a",
            "say": "like the a in father",
            "word": "არა",
            "word_latin": "ara",
            "meaning": "no"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ე",
            "latin": "e",
            "say": "like the e in bed",
            "word": "ერთი",
            "word_latin": "erti",
            "meaning": "one"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ი",
            "latin": "i",
            "say": "like the ee in see, but short",
            "word": "ია",
            "word_latin": "ia",
            "meaning": "violet (the flower)"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ო",
            "latin": "o",
            "say": "like the o in for, but short",
            "word": "ორი",
            "word_latin": "ori",
            "meaning": "two"
          },
          {
            "letter": "უ",
            "latin": "u",
            "say": "like the oo in food, but short",
            "word": "უბანი",
            "word_latin": "ubani",
            "meaning": "neighbourhood"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      },
      {
        "h": "The first consonants"
      },
      "The რ is rolled with the tip of the tongue. The ს is always a hissing s, also between two vowels.",
      {
        "letters": [
          {
            "letter": "მ",
            "latin": "m",
            "say": "like the m in mum",
            "word": "მამა",
            "word_latin": "mama",
            "meaning": "dad"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ნ",
            "latin": "n",
            "say": "like the n in no",
            "word": "ნიორი",
            "word_latin": "niori",
            "meaning": "garlic"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ლ",
            "latin": "l",
            "say": "like the l in lamp",
            "word": "ლომი",
            "word_latin": "lomi",
            "meaning": "lion"
          },
          {
            "letter": "რ",
            "latin": "r",
            "say": "a rolled r, as in Italian or Spanish",
            "word": "რძე",
            "word_latin": "rdze",
            "meaning": "milk"
          },
          {
            "letter": "ს",
            "latin": "s",
            "say": "like the s in sun, never like a z",
            "word": "სახლი",
            "word_latin": "sakhli",
            "meaning": "house"
          }
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      },
      {
        "h": "A tip"
      },
      "Many letters look alike at first: look at where the loops and tails are, and say the sound aloud each time you write a letter. Tick the box under the letters to hide the sounds and test yourself.",
      {
        "h": "Try reading"
      },
      "Read each word aloud, then tap it to check.",
      {
        "flash": [
          [
            "მამა",
            "mama",
            "dad"
          ],
          [
            "ლომი",
            "lomi",
            "lion"
          ],
          [
            "ორი",
            "ori",
            "two"
          ],
          [
            "სამი",
            "sami",
            "three"
          ],
          [
            "მე",
            "me",
            "I, me"
          ],
          [
            "ია",
            "ia",
            "violet"
          ],
          [
            "ლიმონი",
            "limoni",
            "lemon"
          ],
          [
            "მარილი",
            "marili",
            "salt"
          ]
        ],
        "lang": "ka"
      }
    ]
  },
